== 5.3 Safe Planning and Assessment

Begin from the person's experience, goals and circumstances. A suitable warm-up prepares for the activity; recovery and rest are part of the overall plan. Environment, equipment, hydration and supervision also matter. Increase demands appropriately rather than assuming that more is always better.

A fitness test should match the quality it is intended to assess, use a consistent procedure and be interpreted in context. A result is not a diagnosis. Anyone with injury, concerning symptoms or a health condition affecting participation may need individual advice from a qualified professional. Stop activity and seek urgent help when serious symptoms warrant it.

#concept-box("A useful comparison")[
  If a test is repeated to monitor change, keep the procedure and conditions as consistent as practical. An apparent difference may reflect a changed procedure, fatigue or measurement error as well as a change in performance.
]

== 5.4 Four Worked Examples
#worked-example(1, "Joint range", tier: "FOUNDATION",
  [The fitness component most directly concerned with range of movement at a joint is \
A. flexibility \
B. a sports federation \
C. a tendon name \
D. a file format],
  [Flexibility concerns range of movement at a joint. The answer is *A*.])
#worked-example(2, "Repeated effort", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [The ability to repeat or sustain muscular effort is most directly \
A. body composition \
B. muscular endurance \
C. a posture label \
D. reaction time only],
  [Muscular endurance concerns sustaining or repeating effort. The answer is *B*.])
#worked-example(3, "FITT", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [In FITT, how often a person trains describes \
A. type \
B. time \
C. frequency \
D. a diagnosis],
  [Frequency is how often the activity occurs. The answer is *C*.])
#worked-example(4, "Match the goal", tier: "JAMB CHALLENGE",
  [Choosing practice that relates to the skill or activity being improved illustrates \
A. randomisation without a goal \
B. exclusion \
C. an injury diagnosis \
D. specificity],
  [Specificity relates training to the intended adaptation or goal. The answer is *D*.])

#trap-box("Fitness is not one number")[
  Strength and endurance are different; frequency and intensity are different; a test result is not a diagnosis. A plan must account for the individual and context.
]

